      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782233365421,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Guarantee transaction safely and financial integrity\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Guarantee transaction safely and financial integrity\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "I_9vJksq4pnt-dz3zLh4x",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1164.9574433618786,
      "y": 2274.3982776173107,
      "width": 1559.2786865234375,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 968456550,
      "version": 42,
      "versionNonce": 1060880038,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782233427342,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Record the attempt: \n-- Before calling any payment network, we write an attempt record to our database with the network name, reference ID, and what we're trying to accomplish. \nThis triggers a CDC event capturing our intention.\n2. Call the payment network: \nWe send the actual charge request with our configured timeout.\n3. Handle the response (branching based on outcome):\n-- Success: Update the attempt status to \"succeeded\" in the database, \nwhich triggers another CDC event with the successful outcome\n-- Timeout: Update the attempt status to \"timeout\" in the database, \ntriggering a CDC event that the reconciliation service will process\n-- Explicit failure: Update the attempt status to \"failed\" with the failure reason\n4. Automated reconciliation: \n-- A dedicated reconciliation service consumes timeout events \nand proactively queries the payment network using our recorded reference ID \nto determine what actually happened.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Record the attempt: \n-- Before calling any payment network, we write an attempt record to our database with the network name, reference ID, and what we're trying to accomplish. \nThis triggers a CDC event capturing our intention.\n2. Call the payment network: \nWe send the actual charge request with our configured timeout.\n3. Handle the response (branching based on outcome):\n-- Success: Update the attempt status to \"succeeded\" in the database, \nwhich triggers another CDC event with the successful outcome\n-- Timeout: Update the attempt status to \"timeout\" in the database, \ntriggering a CDC event that the reconciliation service will process\n-- Explicit failure: Update the attempt status to \"failed\" with the failure reason\n4. Automated reconciliation: \n-- A dedicated reconciliation service consumes timeout events \nand proactively queries the payment network using our recorded reference ID \nto determine what actually happened.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PQxFtUOH1UqmLo0yk6fYc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1186.6463694677068,
      "y": 2672.342921819908,
      "width": 1018.8992309570312,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1747204198,
      "version": 713,
      "versionNonce": 1310777958,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782233681016,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Scaling\n-- Our services is stateless and will scale horizontally with load balancers in front of them \ndistibuting the load\n-- Kafka: partition kafka topics by payment_inetnt_id, ensures all events\nfor given paymentInent are processed in order while allowing parallel processing across different payment\n-- DB growth -- assume each row is 500byts ==> storing 10000 will be ~500gb ==> ~180TB / year\n-- For transaction that is older than certain period (3-6 months), we could store them in cold storage,\narchived data is still accessible but would not impact operational DB performance. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Scaling\n-- Our services is stateless and will scale horizontally with load balancers in front of them \ndistibuting the load\n-- Kafka: partition kafka topics by payment_inetnt_id, ensures all events\nfor given paymentInent are processed in order while allowing parallel processing across different payment\n-- DB growth -- assume each row is 500byts ==> storing 10000 will be ~500gb ==> ~180TB / year\n-- For transaction that is older than certain period (3-6 months), we could store them in cold storage,\narchived data is still accessible but would not impact operational DB performance. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
